====================================================================================================
FITTED or FREE? separated by quotation, as the prereg requires
====================================================================================================
  A FITTED coefficient is chosen to reproduce an observable value. Entry 59's is not:
  had beta been fitted to the Planck spectral index, the paper would match it. It does not:
    L368: 50–60), we would obtain a value of ns ≈ 0.99, which on face value                         These variations are shown in Figs. 9, 10, and 11 respective
    L369: is in tension with the Planck 2015 best-fit estimate at about 6σ .                         always find a red tilt in the spectrum of scalar perturbati

  The paper reports its own 6-sigma tension with Planck 2015 for standard e-fold counts,
  and rescues it only by adopting a non-standard horizon-crossing scale (N ~ 20-25) or an
  extra relativistic degree of freedom. A fitted parameter would not leave a 6-sigma gap.
  Therefore beta is FREE -- chosen for qualitative behaviour, not fitted to data.

